      <div type="clause" n="29">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 29</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="29" corresp="#wit-e"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.star"/><pb n="64" ed="#liebermann"/>XXIIII. Gif mon twyhyndne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.6"/> mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.7"/> unsynnigne mid hloðe ofslea<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.8"/>, gielde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.9"/> se ðæs sleges<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.10"/> andetta<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.11"/> sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.12"/> wer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.13"/> ⁊ wite; ⁊ æghwelc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.14"/> mon ðe on siðe wære geselle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.15"/> XXX scill. to hloðbote.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.16"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="29" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="62" ed="#liebermann"/>XXIII.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.15-2"/> Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.2"/> twyhyndne mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.2"/> unsynnigne ofslea mid hloþe, gilde se (ðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.1"/>) þæs sleges<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.2"/> ondetta<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.3"/> sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.4"/> wer ⁊ wite; ⁊ æghwylc ðara ðe on ðæm<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.5"/> syþe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.4"/> wære geselle XXX scll' to hloþbote.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="29" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="64" ed="#liebermann"/>Be twyhyndu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> men æt hloðslihte. Gyf man twyhynde man unsynnigne mid hloþe ofsléa, gylde se ðæs slæges andetta sy wer ⁊ wite; ⁊ ælc mon ðe on syþe wære gesylle ðrittig scill' to loðbote.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="29" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="65" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis hominem tƿihindum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.3-2"/> innocentem cum hloðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.4-2"/> (id est cohorte) occidat, reddat qui ictum confitebitur weram et witam; et omnis, qui interfuerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.5-2"/>, reddat XXX sol. de<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.6-2"/> hloþbota.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_29.lnote.oe.4-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="76" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be twyhyndum men æt hloðslihte.] Gif mon twyhyndne mon unsynnigne mid hloðe ofslea, gielde se ðæs<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_29.attnote.fn.1"/> sleges andetta sie wer ⁊ wite; ⁊ æghwelc<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Af_29.attnote.fn.2"/> mon ðe on siðe<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#Af_29.attnote.fn.3"/> wære geselle XXX scill. to hloðbote.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="30" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="322" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XXIIII} Gif mon twyhyndne mon unsynnigne mid hloðe ofslea, gielde se ðæs sleges andetta sie wer ⁊ wite; ⁊ æghwelc mon ðe on siðe wære geselle XXX scill to hloðbote.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="65" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand mit einer Bande<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_29.lnote.de.1"/> einen unschuldigen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_29.lnote.de.2"/> 200-[Schilling-]Mann<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_29.lnote.de.3"/> erschlägt, so zahle, wer des Todtschlags geständig ist, das Wergeld [des Erschlagenen an dessen Sippe] und Strafgeld [an den Richter]; und jeder Mann<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_29.lnote.de.4"/>, der bei [diesem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_29.lnote.de.5"/>] Zuge war, zahle 30<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_29.lnote.de.6"/> Schill. als Bandenbusse.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_29.lnote.de.7"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone with a band slays an innocent 200-[shilling] man, let whoever confesses to the slaying pay the wergeld [of the slain, to his kin] and the fine [to the judge]; and let every man who was on [that] expedition pay 30 shillings as band-compensation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="77" ed="#attenborough"/>If one of a band of marauders<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_29.attnote.n.1"/> slays an unoffending man, whose wergeld is 200 shillings, he who acknowledges the blow shall pay the wergeld and the fine; and everyone engaged in the affair shall pay<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Af_29.attnote.n.2"/> 30 shillings compensation for belonging to such a band.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="413" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone with a band of men kills an innocent man of a two-hundred wergild, he who admits the slaying is to pay the wergild and the fine, and each man who was in that expedition is to pay 30 shillings as compensation for being in that band.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="323" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone in a band slays an innocent 200-[wergild] man, let him who admits the slaying pay <hi rend="italic">wer</hi> and fine; and let each man who was on the expedition add 30 shillings as compensation for taking part in the band.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="280"><label>gloss to</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_13-1">Ine 13.1–15.1</ref> <quote>look like glosses to Ine. Some extended Ine's coverage (n. 78: Af 29 – 31:1/Ine 13:1 – 15:1 (gangs))</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="280"><label>cf. (wergeld enumerations)</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_70">Ine 70</ref> <quote>Alfred enumerated the wergelds ... five times as against Ine's once (n. 80)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="323"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_13-1">Ine 13.1</ref> <quote>Between seven and thirty-five men, according to Ine §14.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="323"><label>contrast</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_34">Ine 34</ref> <quote>Ine §34 sets the higher fine of 50 shillings.</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_29.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Zwischen</hi> 25, 1 <hi rend="italic">und</hi> 29 <hi rend="italic">schiebt</hi> 26 [<hi rend="italic">aber nicht</hi> 27 f.] <hi rend="italic">ein Ld. Um Thorpes und Schmids Zählung beizubehalten, ohne doch mit deren falscher Reihenfolge vom Text abzuweichen, stehen hier die Citirzahlen nicht in arithmetischer Ordnung.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ld inserts 26 [but not 27 f.] between 25, 1 and 29. In order to retain Thorpe’s and Schmid’s numbering without, however, departing from the text by following their incorrect order, the reference numbers here are not in arithmetical order.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_29.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-hindne <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-hindne So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_29.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">man <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">man Ld</seg></note>
