        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_29.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">65</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">pro <hi rend="italic">Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">pro Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_29.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">D. h. mit 7—34 Mann; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Bande 1. 6. 7; gemeinschaftliche Missetat 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">I.e. with 7—34 men; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Bande 1. 6. 7; gemeinschaftliche Missetat 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_29.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Bandenverbrechen tritt also in Ggs. zu erlaubter Fehde in gerechter Blutrache; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Heimsuchung 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Crime by a band is thus set in contrast to lawful feud in just blood-vengeance; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Heimsuchung 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_29.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘D. h. Ceorl’ richtig Inst., auch zu Af 39, 2. Dies Rechtsbuch verbindet III 2 ff. Ine und Eigenes über Bande; <hi rend="italic">o.</hi> I S. 613. — Das Strafgeld für blutig (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 2) Fechten, das der Richter erhält, wechselt nach des Erschlagenen Stand; 31, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘I.e. ceorl’ Inst., rightly, also on Af 39, 2. This law-book combines, in III 2 ff., Ine with its own material on bands; <hi rend="italic">above</hi> I p. 613. — The fine for fighting with bloodshed (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 2), which the judge receives, varies according to the rank of the slain man; 31, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_29.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘von denen’ fügt H zu</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H adds ‘of them’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_29.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H setzt modernisierend Artikel ein</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H inserts the article, modernizing</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_29.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Af ermässigt das Strafgeld für Bandenverbrechen gegen Ine 34, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Af reduces the fine for crime by a band as compared with Ine 34, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_29.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">an den Richter laut Ine 15</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">to the judge, according to Ine 15</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_29.attnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><label>ðæs</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">se (ðe) þæs</hi>. H*.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_29.attnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><label>æghwelc</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ælc</hi>. B. <hi rend="italic">æghwylc þara</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_29.attnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><label>siðe</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ðæm syþe</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_29.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">196</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">For a definition of <hi rend="italic">hloþ</hi>, see Ine, cap. 13 § 1.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_29.attnote.n.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">196</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. Ine, cap. 34 § 1, where the penalties are somewhat different.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Af_29.whinote.n.1" n="1" source="#whitelock" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">413</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The figures in brackets are those retained by Liebermann from earlier editors who rearranged the MS. order. Attenborough numbers straight on.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The word her note number follows ((29).) was not found in this row; the note is on the clause as a whole.</note></note>
